{"id":"mahabharata-3-291","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":291,"title":"एकनवत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 291 · The Sun's promise to Kunti","summary":{"en":"Kunti pleads her maidenhood and her family's honour, but the Sun threatens to burn her father and the Brahmin if she refuses. He promises that she will remain a virgin and that her son will be born with divine armour and earrings, and, entering her by yoga, he gives her the child without touching her.","kn":"ಕುಂತಿ ತನ್ನ ಕನ್ಯಾತ್ವ ಮತ್ತು ಕುಲಗೌರವವನ್ನು ಮುಂದಿಡುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ಆದರೆ ನಿರಾಕರಿಸಿದರೆ ತಂದೆ ಮತ್ತು ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನನ್ನು ಸುಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಸೂರ್ಯನು ಬೆದರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅವಳು ಕನ್ಯೆಯಾಗಿಯೇ ಉಳಿಯುವಳು, ಮಗ ದಿವ್ಯ ಕವಚ ಕುಂಡಲಗಳೊಂದಿಗೆ ಹುಟ್ಟುವನು ಎಂದು ವಾಗ್ದಾನ ಮಾಡಿ ಯೋಗದಿಂದ ಅವಳನ್ನು ಪ್ರವೇಶಿಸಿ ಸ್ಪರ್ಶಿಸದೆ ಗರ್ಭ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कुन्ती अपने कौमार्य और कुल के सम्मान की दुहाई देती हैं, पर सूर्य धमकाते हैं कि मना करने पर वे उनके पिता और ब्राह्मण को जला देंगे। वे वचन देते हैं कि वे कुमारी ही रहेंगी और उनका पुत्र दिव्य कवच-कुण्डल के साथ जन्मेगा, और योग से उनमें प्रवेश कर बिना स्पर्श किए गर्भ देते हैं।","te":"కుంతి తన కన్యాత్వాన్ని, కుల గౌరవాన్ని ముందుపెడుతుంది, కానీ నిరాకరిస్తే తండ్రిని, బ్రాహ్మణుని కాల్చివేస్తానని సూర్యుడు బెదిరిస్తాడు. ఆమె కన్యగానే ఉంటుందని, కుమారుడు దివ్య కవచకుండలాలతో పుడతాడని వాగ్దానం చేసి యోగంతో ఆమెలో ప్రవేశించి తాకకుండానే గర్భం ఇస్తాడు.","ta":"குந்தி தன் கன்னிமையையும் குலப் பெருமையையும் எடுத்துரைக்க, மறுத்தால் அவள் தந்தையையும் அந்தணரையும் எரிப்பேன் என்று சூரியன் அச்சுறுத்துகிறான். அவள் கன்னியாகவே இருப்பாள், மகன் தெய்வீகக் கவச குண்டலங்களுடன் பிறப்பான் என்று வாக்களித்து, யோகத்தால் அவளுள் புகுந்து தொடாமலேயே கருவை அளிக்கிறான்.","ml":"കന്യകാത്വവും കുടുംബത്തിന്റെ മാനവും കുന്തി അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; പക്ഷേ അവൾ വിസമ്മതിച്ചാൽ പിതാവിനെയും ബ്രാഹ്മണനെയും ദഹിപ്പിക്കുമെന്ന് സൂര്യൻ ഭീഷണിപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു. അവൾ കന്യകയായി തുടരുമെന്നും, ദിവ്യകവചവും കുണ്ഡലങ്ങളുമായി അവളുടെ പുത്രൻ ജനിക്കുമെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു; യോഗത്തിലൂടെ അവളിൽ പ്രവേശിച്ച് അവളെ സ്പർശിക്കാതെ അദ്ദേഹം കുട്ടിയെ നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.291; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कुण्डलाहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Kundalaharana Parva (Taking of the earrings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सा तु कन्या बहुविधं ब्रुवन्ती मधुरं वचः ।\nअनुनेतुं सहस्रांशुं न शशाक मनस्विनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The proud girl, speaking in many sweet ways, could not persuade the thousand-rayed god to leave."}},{"n":2,"text":"न शशाक यदा बाला प्रत्याख्यातुं तमोनुदम् ।\nभीता शापात्ततो राजन्दध्यौ दीर्घमथान्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the girl could not refuse the dispeller of darkness, king, she grew afraid of his curse and fell into a long inner anxiety."}},{"n":3,"text":"अनागसः पितुः शापो ब्राह्मणस्य तथैव च ।\nमन्निमित्तः कथं न स्यात्क्रुद्धादस्माद्विभावसोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How could the curse of that angry lord of light not fall, because of me, on my innocent father and on the brahmin?"}},{"n":4,"text":"बालेनापि सता मोहाद्भृशं सापह्नवान्यपि ।\nनात्यासादयितव्यानि तेजांसि च तपांसि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a child, if good, must not too much approach radiances and austerities through ignorance, even when they can be denied."}},{"n":5,"text":"साहमद्य भृशं भीता गृहीता च करे भृशम् ।\nकथं त्वकार्यं कुर्यां वै प्रदानं ह्यात्मनः स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today I am terrified, and gripped hard by the hand; how can I do the forbidden thing, giving myself away on my own?"}},{"n":6,"text":"सैवं शापपरित्रस्ता बहु चिन्तयती तदा ।\nमोहेनाभिपरीताङ्गी स्मयमाना पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, frightened of the curse, thinking much, her limbs seized by bewilderment, she smiled again and again."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं देवमब्रवीद्भीता बन्धूनां राजसत्तम ।\nव्रीडाविह्वलया वाचा शापत्रस्ता विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Afraid, best of kings, with a voice shaken by shame, she spoke to the god out of concern for her kinsmen, trembling at the curse, lord of the people."}},{"text":"कुन्त्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kunti said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"पिता मे ध्रियते देव माता चान्ये च बान्धवाः ।\nन तेषु ध्रियमाणेषु विधिलोपो भवेदयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"My father is alive, god, and my mother and other relatives; while they live, this should not be a violation of the rule."}},{"n":9,"text":"त्वया मे संगमो देव यदि स्याद्विधिवर्जितः ।\nमन्निमित्तं कुलस्यास्य लोके कीर्तिर्नशेत्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If a union with you, god, should occur against the rule, then because of me the fame of this family would be lost in the world."}},{"n":10,"text":"अथ वा धर्ममेतं त्वं मन्यसे तपतां वर ।\nऋते प्रदानाद्बन्धुभ्यस्तव कामं करोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or if you consider this righteous, best of the burning ones, I would do your wish even without being given by my relatives."}},{"n":11,"text":"आत्मप्रदानं दुर्धर्ष तव कृत्वा सती त्वहम् ।\nत्वयि धर्मो यशश्चैव कीर्तिरायुश्च देहिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having given myself to you, unassailable one, as a chaste woman, in you rest righteousness, glory, fame and the life of embodied beings."}},{"text":"सूर्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Surya said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"न ते पिता न ते माता गुरवो वा शुचिस्मिते ।\nप्रभवन्ति वरारोहे भद्रं ते शृणु मे वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither your father nor your mother nor your elders have authority over you, bright-smiling lady. Good fortune to you; hear my words."}},{"n":13,"text":"सर्वान्कामयते यस्मात्कनेर्धातोश्च भामिनि ।\nतस्मात्कन्येह सुश्रोणि स्वतन्त्रा वरवर्णिनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because she desires all, from the root kan, therefore a kanya, lady with lovely hips, is free here, lovely one."}},{"n":14,"text":"नाधर्मश्चरितः कश्चित्त्वया भवति भामिनि ।\nअधर्मं कुत एवाहं चरेयं लोककाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have committed no wrong, lady. How could I do wrong, I who desire the good of the world?"}},{"n":15,"text":"अनावृताः स्त्रियः सर्वा नराश्च वरवर्णिनि ।\nस्वभाव एष लोकानां विकारोऽन्य इति स्मृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All women and men, lovely lady, are unrestricted; this is the nature of the world, and anything else is called a distortion."}},{"n":16,"text":"सा मया सह संगम्य पुनः कन्या भविष्यसि ।\nपुत्रश्च ते महाबाहुर्भविष्यति महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After uniting with me you will be a maiden again, and you will have a mighty-armed, greatly renowned son."}},{"text":"कुन्त्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kunti said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"यदि पुत्रो मम भवेत्त्वत्तः सर्वतमोपह ।\nकुण्डली कवची शूरो महाबाहुर्महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If I am to have a son from you, dispeller of all darkness, let him be a hero with earrings and armor, mighty-armed and mighty."}},{"text":"सूर्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Surya said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"भविष्यति महाबाहुः कुण्डली दिव्यवर्मभृत् ।\nउभयं चामृतमयं तस्य भद्रे भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"He will be mighty-armed, with earrings and divine armor; both of these will be made of nectar, good lady."}},{"text":"कुन्त्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kunti said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"यद्येतदमृतादस्ति कुण्डले वर्म चोत्तमम् ।\nमम पुत्रस्य यं वै त्वं मत्त उत्पादयिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the earrings and the excellent armor are from nectar, for my son whom you will beget on me,"}},{"n":20,"text":"अस्तु मे संगमो देव यथोक्तं भगवंस्त्वया ।\nत्वद्वीर्यरूपसत्त्वौजा धर्मयुक्तो भवेत्स च ॥","meaning":{"en":"then let the union be, god, as you have said, lord; and may he, endowed with your valor, form, strength and vigor, be righteous."}},{"text":"सूर्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Surya said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"अदित्या कुण्डले राज्ञि दत्ते मे मत्तकाशिनि ।\nतेऽस्य दास्यामि वै भीरु वर्म चैवेदमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Queen, the earrings and this excellent armor were given to me by Aditi, you who are intoxicated by youth; I will give them to him, timid one."}},{"text":"पृथोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Pritha said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"परमं भगवन्देव संगमिष्ये त्वया सह ।\nयदि पुत्रो भवेदेवं यथा वदसि गोपते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, supreme lord and god, I will unite with you, if the son will be as you say, lord of rays."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":23,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वा तु तां कुन्तीमाविवेश विहंगमः ।\nस्वर्भानुशत्रुर्योगात्मा नाभ्यां पस्पर्श चैव ताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying, So be it, the sky-goer, enemy of Svarbhanu, whose self is yoga, entered Kunti and touched her navel."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततः सा विह्वलेवासीत्कन्या सूर्यस्य तेजसा ।\nपपाताथ च सा देवी शयने मूढचेतना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the girl, overwhelmed by Surya's radiance, became as if faint, and the lady fell on her bed with a bewildered mind."}},{"text":"सूर्य उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Surya said:"}},{"n":25,"text":"साधयिष्यामि सुश्रोणि पुत्रं वै जनयिष्यसि ।\nसर्वशस्त्रभृतां श्रेष्ठं कन्या चैव भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will accomplish it, fair-hipped one: you will bear a son, best of all who bear weapons, and you will be a maiden still."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः सा व्रीडिता बाला तदा सूर्यमथाब्रवीत् ।\nएवमस्त्विति राजेन्द्र प्रस्थितं भूरिवर्चसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, ashamed, the girl said to the very radiant Surya, as he was leaving, So be it, king of kings."}},{"n":27,"text":"इति स्मोक्ता कुन्तिराजात्मजा सा\nविवस्वन्तं याचमाना सलज्जा ।\nतस्मिन्पुण्ये शयनीये पपात\nमोहाविष्टा भज्यमाना लतेव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the daughter of the Kunti king, begging Vivasvan, ashamed, fell on that sacred bed, overwhelmed, like a creeper being broken."}},{"n":28,"text":"तां तिग्मांशुस्तेजसा मोहयित्वा\nयोगेनाविश्यात्मसंस्थां चकार ।\nन चैवैनां दूषयामास भानुः\nसंज्ञां लेभे भूय एवाथ बाला ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sharp-rayed one, stupefying her with his radiance and entering her by yoga, placed himself within her; but the sun did not defile her, and the girl regained her senses."}}]}]}